 "title": "Do bulls really hate red? Total myth 🐂",
 "description": "Bulls are red-green colour blind, and in a 2007 TV test a bull charged red, blue and white flags alike, then chased moving cowboys and ignored a man in red standing still. It's the movement, not the colour.\n\nSources: Live Science, 'Why Do Bulls Charge When They See Red?'; Mental Floss, 'What Really Happens If You Wear Red in Front of a Bull?'; Ripley's, 'Seeing Red: Bulls Don't Care About Red'.",
